Example 1 — Mobile app, detailed, phases_table:

Input project_description:
"Mobile app for booking medical appointments on iOS and Android, login,
calendar with availability, push reminders, integration with a single external
EMR via REST."

Expected JSON:
{
  "summary": "Native mobile app on iOS and Android for booking medical appointments. The plan is broken into the phases below: discovery and architecture, authentication and onboarding, calendar core, EMR integration, and hardening. See `phases` for the canonical breakdown.",
  "total_duration_weeks": 22,
  "total_cost_eur": 132000,
  "confidence_pct": 78,
  "phases": [
    {
      "name": "Discovery and architecture",
      "duration_weeks": 3,
      "cost_eur": 18000,
      "confidence_pct": 85,
      "assumptions": [
        "Single product manager and one tech lead allocated full-time",
        "EMR API documentation available before kickoff",
        "iOS 16+ and Android 12+ as minimum supported versions",
        "App store accounts and signing certificates already provisioned",
        "Design system reused from an existing internal app"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Authentication and onboarding",
      "duration_weeks": 4,
      "cost_eur": 24000,
      "confidence_pct": 80,
      "assumptions": [
        "Email + password plus social login (Google, Apple)",
        "No biometric login in v1",
        "Standard onboarding: 3 screens + permissions",
        "Backend auth delegated to a managed provider (Auth0 or Cognito)",
        "Push notification setup limited to FCM and APNs defaults"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Calendar core",
      "duration_weeks": 8,
      "cost_eur": 48000,
      "confidence_pct": 75,
      "assumptions": [
        "One doctor profile model with availability slots",
        "Booking model with cancellation policy (24h window)",
        "Timezone handling defaults to device timezone",
        "Recurring availability supported via simple weekly rules",
        "No multi-resource booking (rooms, equipment) in v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "EMR integration",
      "duration_weeks": 5,
      "cost_eur": 30000,
      "confidence_pct": 70,
      "assumptions": [
        "Single EMR vendor, REST/JSON API",
        "Read-only on patient data; write only on appointments",
        "Retry-with-backoff for transient errors",
        "Mapping table maintained in the backend, not on the device",
        "Sandbox credentials available from week 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Hardening, beta and store submission",
      "duration_weeks": 2,
      "cost_eur": 12000,
      "confidence_pct": 80,
      "assumptions": [
        "Closed beta with 25 internal users",
        "One round of accessibility audit (WCAG AA)",
        "App store review buffer of one week absorbed within the phase",
        "Crash reporting via Sentry",
        "No staged rollout automation beyond default app store options"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

Example 2 — Web SaaS, medium, line_items:

Input project_description:
"Internal SaaS dashboard for a fintech compliance team: list of flagged
transactions, filters, export to CSV, role-based access."

Expected JSON:
{
  "summary": "Internal compliance dashboard for a fintech team, scoped to a single tenant and roughly 12 weeks of work at ~78k EUR. The plan covers the data ingestion contract, the dashboard surface, role-based access, and an export pipeline; the audit log and SSO are explicitly out of scope for v1.",
  "total_duration_weeks": 12,
  "total_cost_eur": 78000,
  "confidence_pct": 72,
  "phases": [
    {
      "name": "Ingestion contract and read API",
      "duration_weeks": 3,
      "cost_eur": 19500,
      "confidence_pct": 75,
      "assumptions": [
        "Source system exposes flagged-transaction events on a queue",
        "Read API exposes filterable list endpoints",
        "Postgres single-tenant database with row-level filters",
        "No retention policy implemented in v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dashboard frontend",
      "duration_weeks": 4,
      "cost_eur": 26000,
      "confidence_pct": 70,
      "assumptions": [
        "Single SPA using the existing internal design system",
        "Filters: date range, status, amount, currency",
        "Server-side pagination with cursor",
        "No real-time updates; manual refresh button"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Role-based access",
      "duration_weeks": 2,
      "cost_eur": 13000,
      "confidence_pct": 75,
      "assumptions": [
        "Three roles: viewer, analyst, admin",
        "Permissions evaluated server-side on every request",
        "Admin role can change role assignments via internal CLI in v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "CSV export and hardening",
      "duration_weeks": 3,
      "cost_eur": 19500,
      "confidence_pct": 70,
      "assumptions": [
        "Export caps at 50k rows synchronously, async beyond that",
        "Sentry for errors; basic structured logs",
        "No PDF export, no scheduled reports",
        "Manual QA pass at the end of the phase"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

